# 3. THE CORE 3D HUMAN ANATOMY EXPERIENCE
This is the most important part of the entire product.
The main application must feature a large, interactive, detailed 3D human anatomical model.
The user must be able to:
### 3.1 Rotate
- Rotate the human body horizontally.
- Rotate vertically where technically appropriate.
- Inspect the front, back, left, right, and other angles.
- Use mouse drag on desktop.
- Use touch gestures on mobile.
- Maintain smooth camera movement.
### 3.2 Zoom
- Zoom in and out smoothly.
- Inspect small anatomical structures.
- Zoom towards the selected structure where practical.
- Support mouse-wheel zoom.
- Support mobile pinch-to-zoom.
### 3.3 Pan
- Move the camera around the model.
- Reposition the model within the viewing area.
- Provide an easy way to reset the camera.
### 3.4 Select anatomical structures
Users should be able to click or tap an anatomical structure.
When selected:
- Visually highlight the selected structure.
- Display its correct anatomical name.
- Display relevant educational information.
- Show its anatomical system.
- Provide access to more detailed information.
- Keep the selected structure visually distinguishable from surrounding structures.
Selection must work with the actual 3D geometry, not just decorative buttons.
### 3.5 Isolate structures
Where supported by the underlying model:
- Isolate an individual structure.
- Hide surrounding structures.
- Restore the complete body.
- Highlight a selected structure.
- Make surrounding structures transparent.
- Control the visibility of anatomical systems.
### 3.6 Anatomical model controls
Include:
- Reset camera
- Front view
- Back view
- Left view
- Right view
- Zoom in
- Zoom out
- Show/hide structures
- Isolate selection
- Restore full model
- Fullscreen viewer
Make these controls intuitive and accessible.
### 3.7 Anatomical model quality
Use the highest-quality usable existing anatomical meshes available in the inspected repositories.
Do not replace detailed models with:
- Flat illustrations
- Static pictures
- Cartoon human figures
- Generic geometric shapes
- Unrelated 3D objects
The 3D human anatomy model must be the central feature of the application.
